# Stonecutter rewrites the working tree in place for whichever version is active, so every file here is
# one a preprocessor may rewrite. Line endings have to be settled before that starts: a checkout that
# flips CRLF and LF turns a one-line preprocessor change into a whole-file diff, and produces merge
# conflicts in files nobody touched.
#
# The index is already all-LF -- core.autocrlf has been doing that work on this machine. This makes it a
# property of the repository instead, so it holds for CI and for anyone who clones it. Nothing is staged
# by adding this: a working-tree file converts on its next checkout, and normalises back to what the
# index already holds.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The one consumer that still wants CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never inspected, never converted. Content detection would catch these anyway; naming the three kinds
# this repository actually holds is cheaper than discovering that one of them was not caught.
*.png binary
*.jar binary
*.nbt binary
